    <bpmn:process id="W_W215" name="W215. Customer Home Delivery Reverse Logistics (Returns)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests return or exchange for an item delivered to their home (W19/W19B)
Frequency: ~3–7% of home delivery orders (the courier-pickup leg of the ecommerce returns canon: ≈ 4,000–5,000 total return requests/month per W1623, less the ≈ 3,300–4,200 store drop-offs per W12B)
Volume: ~800–1,700 returns/month at steady state (the courier-pickup remainder of the W1623 canon; peaks post-holiday and post-promo)
Owner: Ecommerce Customer Service Manager
Participants: Customer, CSR, 3PL Carrier, DC Receiving Team, Finance (Refunds)
Source: workflow W215 — Customer Home Delivery Reverse Logistics (Returns)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W215_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane2" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane3" name="3PL Carrier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane4" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane5" name="Quality Checker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane6" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W215_Lane7" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W215_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W215_Start9" name="Customer requests return or exchange for an item delivered to their home (W19/W19B)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task10" name="Return Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Return Request: Customer initiates return via Web/App or Call Center; provides reason and photos of item/packaging
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task11" name="Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Validation: CSR reviews request against Return Policy (W12); verifies purchase date and item condition; approves for pickup
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W215_Task12" name="Collection Booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Collection Booking: System books 3PL carrier (Lalamove/Transportify) for home pickup; generates &quot;Return Label&quot; for customer
Responsible (R): CSR / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task13" name="Pick-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pick-up: Carrier collects item from customer; verifies &quot;Return ID&quot; and basic condition; issues &quot;Proof of Collection&quot;
Responsible (R): 3PL Carrier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task14" name="DC Receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DC Receipt: Item arrives at DC (or Hub); Receiving Clerk scans Return Label; system identifies original Order/SO
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task15" name="Quality Inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quality Inspection: Quality Checker inspects item: (a) Resaleable → return to stock (W91); (b) Damaged → quarantine (W91); (c) Wrong item → flag for investigation
Responsible (R): Quality Checker
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W215_Task16" name="Refund Authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Refund Authorization: Once receipt is confirmed and QC passed: Finance authorizes refund to original payment method (W101)
Responsible (R): Finance (AR)
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W215_Task17" name="Closure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Closure: System notifies customer of refund status; updates inventory and sales analytics
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W215_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W215_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W215_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W215_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-270 (ensure controlled execution — Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery (PA-10.2).) | - operational: Ecommerce Customer Service Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Ecommerce Customer Service Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
