    <bpmn:process id="W_W829" name="W829. Customer Ecommerce Order Split &amp; Partial Delivery Proactive Communication" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ecommerce order requires splitting across multiple fulfillment locations per POS-021 multi-DC order splitting
Frequency: Daily; ~15–25% of ecommerce orders require splitting (~6,500–10,700 orders/month)
Volume: ~6,500–10,700 split orders/month out of ~42,900 total; average 2.1 sub-orders per split order
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Specialist
Participants: Operations Specialist, DC Planner, Customer, 3PL Carrier, Customer Service Agent
Source: workflow W829 — Customer Ecommerce Order Split &amp; Partial Delivery Proactive Communication</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W829_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W829_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W829_Lane2" name="Customer Service Agent">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W829_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Ops Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W829_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W829_Start5" name="Ecommerce order requires splitting across multiple fulfillment locations per POS-021…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task6" name="Order split detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Order split detection: system detects order requires split per POS-021: creates sub-orders with separate tracking numbers but unified customer order reference
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task7" name="Immediate customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Immediate customer notification: system sends W708 communication within 5 minutes of order confirmation: (a) &quot;Your order has been split for faster fulfillment&quot; — positive framing; (b) list of items per delivery with estimated delivery dates; (c) separate tracking numbers per sub-order; (d) total amount remains same — no additional charges; (e) single point of contact for any questions per W258
Responsible (R): System / Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: &lt; 5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task8" name="Sub-order routing to DCs">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sub-order routing to DCs: system routes sub-orders to respective DCs per W536 unified order management: (a) DC1 fulfills items A, B, C; (b) DC3 fulfills items D, E; (c) each DC picks, packs, and dispatches per W106
Responsible (R): System / DC Planner
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: Automated routing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task9" name="Sub-order status tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sub-order status tracking: customer sees unified order dashboard: (a) overall order status (% complete by items); (b) individual sub-order status with carrier tracking per W592; (c) delivered items checked off; (d) pending items with countdown to delivery
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: Continuous (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task10" name="First delivery notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: First delivery notification: system sends notification — &quot;Part 1 of your order has been delivered! Items D and E are on their way, estimated [date]&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task11" name="Partial delivery gap monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Partial delivery gap monitoring: if more than 3 days between first and last sub-order delivery: (a) system sends proactive status update; (b) if any sub-order delayed beyond estimated date: W708 notification with updated ETA and apology; (c) Customer Service preemptively available for inquiries per W259
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Agent
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: 15-30 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W829_Task12" name="Final delivery confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Final delivery confirmation: system sends &quot;Your order is complete!&quot; notification with: (a) delivery confirmation for all items; (b) feedback/review prompt per W510; (c) related product recommendations per W156 CDP
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W829_Task13" name="Exception handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Exception handling: (a) if one sub-order is cancelled (out of stock after split): immediate customer notification, refund for affected items per W101, option to cancel remaining sub-orders; (b) if customer wants to return items from only one sub-order: process per W215 returns with sub-order reference
Responsible (R): Customer Service Agent / Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 30 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W829_Task14" name="Monthly split order analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Monthly split order analytics: (a) split order rate; (b) average sub-orders per split; (c) delivery gap statistics; (d) split order complaint rate vs. non-split; (e) customer satisfaction comparison; (f) SKU availability by DC to identify inventory positioning improvements per W183
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Specialist
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W829_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W829_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W829_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W829_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-270 (ensure controlled execution — Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery (PA-10.2).) | - operational: Ecommerce Operations Specialist review and approval gate
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Specialist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W829_Assoc17" sourceRef="W829_Annotation16" targetRef="W829_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W829_Flow18" sourceRef="W829_Start5" targetRef="W829_Task6" />
