    <bpmn:process id="W_W1196" name="W1196. Ship-from-Store Fulfillment Operations &amp; Store-Level Inventory Reservation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ecommerce order is routed to a store for fulfillment (home delivery or BOPIS)
Frequency: ~1,500–2,800 ship-from-store orders/month (stores serve as fulfillment nodes for bulky and local-availability items; per W19B/W591)
Volume: ~7–14 ship-from-store orders/store/month (~1,500–2,800/month chain-wide, per the Frequency)
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Stock Associate (store picker), Store Manager, Ecommerce Ops Manager, 3PL Delivery Partner
Source: workflow W1196 — Ship-from-Store Fulfillment Operations &amp; Store-Level Inventory Reservation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1196_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1196_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1196_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1196_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1196_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1196_Start5" name="Ecommerce order is routed to a store for fulfillment (home delivery or BOPIS)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1196_Task6" name="Order routing to store">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Order routing to store: Ecommerce system routes order to nearest store with available inventory; system considers: (a) item availability (real-time store inventory from POS sync), (b) store operating hours, (c) item type restrictions (hazardous items per W82 cannot be shipped from store via standard courier — only customer pickup or specialized carrier), (d) store fulfillment capacity (daily pick capacity threshold); system pushes order to store&#x27;s fulfillment queue on handheld tablet
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1196_Task7" name="Inventory reservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inventory reservation: Upon order routing: system reserves inventory at the store (decrements available-to-promise quantity but not physical inventory until pick); reservation holds for 4 hours (BOPIS) or until end of business day (delivery); if not picked within hold period, reservation expires and order is rerouted to alternate store or DC
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1196_Task8" name="Pick list generation and assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pick list generation and assignment: System generates digital pick list on store tablet with: (a) item SKU, description, and quantity, (b) aisle/shelf location, (c) item image for verification; assigns to available Stock Associate based on current workload; Stock Associate receives push notification
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1196_Task9" name="In-store picking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: In-store picking: Stock Associate picks items from shelf using handheld scanner; scans each item barcode to confirm correct SKU and lot/batch; if item not found at designated location: (a) searches nearby locations, (b) if confirmed out of stock: marks as &quot;Pick Failed,&quot; system releases reservation and routes to alternate fulfillment origin; picks bulky items (lumber, cement) from lumber yard or backroom staging area
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–25 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1196_Task10" name="Packing and label generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Packing and label generation: Stock Associate packs items at designated packing station: (a) standard items in corrugated box with void fill, (b) fragile items (tiles) with edge protection, (c) bulky items (lumber) wrapped and labeled; system generates shipping label with customer address and tracking barcode; for hazardous items: applies required DG labels per transport regulations
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–15 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1196_Task11" name="Courier handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Courier handoff: 3PL courier arrives at store per daily pickup schedule; Stock Associate hands off packed orders; courier scans each package for chain-of-custody tracking; system updates order status to &quot;Shipped&quot; and triggers customer notification with tracking number; for BOPIS: customer arrives, CSR verifies identity, releases order
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Courier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/handoff</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1196_Task12" name="End-of-day reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: End-of-day reconciliation: Store Manager reviews daily fulfillment dashboard: (a) orders received vs. orders fulfilled, (b) pick failure rate (target: &lt; 3%), (c) average pick-to-ship time, (d) inventory accuracy exceptions triggered by pick failures; pick failures feed into cycle count priorities per W6
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Manager
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1196_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1196_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1196_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1196_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-270 (ensure controlled execution — Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery (PA-10.2).) | - operational: inventory reservation in Step 2 and prioritizing cycle counts for high-velocity ecommerce items per W6; operational: scheduling picks during off-peak hours (morning before 10 AM) and capping daily store fulfillment volume; operational: routing bulky items to customer pickup (BOPIS) or specialized heavy-haul delivery partners per W1191
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1196_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1196_Annotation14" targetRef="W1196_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
