    <bpmn:process id="W_W1273" name="W1273. Customer E-Commerce In-Store Return Drop-Off Processing &amp; Cross-Channel Refund" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer brings an ecommerce purchase to a BuildRight store for return, having initiated the return online (RMA) or walking in without prior online initiation
Frequency: ~3,300–4,200 ecommerce store drop-offs/month (~8–10% of ~42,900 ecommerce orders — the store drop-off subset of the ≈ 4,000–5,000 total ecommerce return requests per the W1623 canon; ≈ 17–21 drop-offs/store/month)
Volume: ~17–21 in-store ecommerce return drop-offs per store per month; ~3,300–4,200 chain-wide/month (the W12B canon; the courier-pickup remainder ≈ 800–1,700/month rides W215)
Owner: Customer Service Rep
Participants: CSR, Store Manager (approval override), Department Supervisor (quality inspection), Ecommerce Operations (system verification)
Source: workflow W1273 — Customer E-Commerce In-Store Return Drop-Off Processing &amp; Cross-Channel Refund</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1273_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1273_Lane1" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1273_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1273_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1273_Start4" name="Customer brings an ecommerce purchase to a BuildRight store for return, having initiated…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1273_Task5" name="Customer arrival and identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer arrival and identification: customer arrives at Customer Service Counter with item to return; CSR greets customer and asks: (a) &quot;Was this purchased online or in-store?&quot; — if in-store, process per standard W12, (b) if online: &quot;Do you have your order number or return authorization (RMA)?&quot; — customer provides order number (from email confirmation or order history in app), RMA number (if initiated online), or QR code from return confirmation email, (c) if customer has no order reference: CSR looks up order by customer name, email, phone number, or loyalty account
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1273_Task6" name="Order verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Order verification: CSR retrieves ecommerce order in system: (a) confirms order exists and is within return window (standard: 14 days from delivery; extended during holidays: 30 days), (b) verifies item being returned matches an item on the order (SKU, quantity), (c) checks return eligibility: (i) item is returnable per category policy (custom-cut items, paint-mixed items, and installed items may be non-returnable), (ii) item has not been previously returned, (iii) order was not flagged for fraud, (d) if customer has pre-approved RMA: system shows RMA status as &quot;Approved — Awaiting Drop-Off&quot;; CSR proceeds to step 3, (e) if no RMA: CSR initiates RMA in system on customer&#x27;s behalf
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1273_Task7" name="Item inspection and grading">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Item inspection and grading: CSR inspects returned item per W509 grading criteria: (a) Grade A (Resaleable): item in original packaging, unused, all accessories included, no damage — can be returned to store shelf, (b) Grade B (Discountable): item opened, minor cosmetic damage, missing non-critical accessories — can be sold as open-box per W549, (c) Grade C (Non-Resaleable): item used, damaged, missing critical components — RTV to vendor per W88, DC return per W176, or scrap, (d) Grade D (Hazardous/Recall): item poses safety risk — quarantine per W29 recall procedures; CSR records grade in system with photos (mandatory for Grade B and C)
Responsible (R): CSR / Department Supervisor (Grade C/D)
Accountable (A): Store Manager (Grade C/D)
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1273_Task8" name="Refund method determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Refund method determination: system determines refund method based on original payment: (a) Credit/Debit Card → refund to original card (processed by system; 3–5 business days for customer to see credit), (b) E-Wallet (GCash/Maya) → refund to original e-wallet account (processed by system; 1–2 business days), (c) COD (Cash on Delivery) → store credit (gift card per W28) or bank transfer (requires customer to provide bank details), (d) Bank Transfer / Online Banking → refund to original bank account (3–5 business days), (e) Loyalty Points → points restored to customer account immediately; CSR confirms refund method with customer
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1273_Task9" name="Refund processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Refund processing: CSR processes return in system: (a) system creates return transaction linked to original ecommerce order, (b) inventory adjusted: item received into store inventory at appropriate grade (Grade A → saleable stock, Grade B → open-box stock, Grade C → RTV stock), (c) refund initiated to original payment method per step 4, (d) customer signs return receipt (digital signature on tablet or printed), (e) CSR provides customer with return confirmation (printed receipt + email confirmation), (f) if customer prefers exchange: CSR offers store credit or direct exchange for same/different item per W12 exchange rules
Responsible (R): CSR / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager (refund &gt; PHP 10K)
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1273_Task10" name="Cross-channel inventory disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cross-channel inventory disposition: system routes returned item based on grade: (a) Grade A: item added to store inventory — available for sale at this store location immediately, (b) Grade B: item added to store inventory with &quot;Open-Box&quot; status per W549 — discounted pricing applied automatically, (c) Grade C: item flagged for disposition — consolidated with store-level returns per W176 (store-to-DC reverse logistics) for DC-level RTV processing per W88, (d) system updates ecommerce platform inventory availability if item was originally fulfilled from DC (DC stock does not increase; store stock increases)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1273_Task11" name="Ecommerce order status update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Ecommerce order status update: system updates ecommerce order status: (a) order status changes to &quot;Returned — In Store&quot;, (b) customer notification sent: email + SMS confirming return receipt and refund timeline, (c) ecommerce fulfillment metrics updated: return rate, return reason, return grade distribution, (d) if refund is store credit: gift card/voucher generated per W28 and delivered to customer (physical card in-store or digital to email/app)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1273_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1273_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1273_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1273_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-270 (ensure controlled execution — Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery (PA-10.2).) | - operational: Customer Service Representative review and approval gate
Owner: Customer Service Rep</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1273_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1273_Annotation13" targetRef="W1273_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow15" sourceRef="W1273_Start4" targetRef="W1273_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow16" sourceRef="W1273_Task5" targetRef="W1273_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow17" sourceRef="W1273_Task6" targetRef="W1273_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow18" sourceRef="W1273_Task7" targetRef="W1273_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow19" sourceRef="W1273_Task8" targetRef="W1273_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow20" sourceRef="W1273_Task9" targetRef="W1273_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow21" sourceRef="W1273_Task10" targetRef="W1273_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1273_Flow22" sourceRef="W1273_Task11" targetRef="W1273_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1273_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1273_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1273">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1273_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1273_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
