    <bpmn:process id="W_W1429" name="W1429. E-Commerce BOPIS Same-Day Pick SLA Monitoring, Exception Escalation &amp; Customer Notification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BOPIS order placed on ecommerce platform; or SLA breach event (order not ready within 4-hour SLA per model company profile)
Frequency: ~25,700 BOPIS orders/month (~860/day across 200 stores); SLA monitoring continuous; exception escalation as needed
Volume: ~860 BOPIS orders/day; SLA target: 95%+ picked within 4 hours; expected SLA breach rate: 5–8% (~43–69 orders/day needing exception handling)
Owner: E-Commerce Operations Manager
Participants: E-Commerce Operations Manager, Store Stock Associate (picker), Customer Service Rep (store), Store Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W1429 — E-Commerce BOPIS Same-Day Pick SLA Monitoring, Exception Escalation &amp; Customer Notification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1429_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1429_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1429_Lane2" name="E-Commerce Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1429_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1429_Start4" name="BOPIS order placed on ecommerce platform; or SLA breach event (order not ready within…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1429_Task5" name="Order-to-store routing and pick assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Order-to-store routing and pick assignment (T+0): (a) system routes BOPIS order to designated store based on: (i) item availability (near-real-time inventory per W525), (ii) store proximity to customer&#x27;s selected pickup location, (iii) store pick queue depth (distribute orders across stores with capacity), (b) store receives pick list on Stock Associate&#x27;s RF device: items, quantities, bin locations, SLA deadline (order time + 4 hours), (c) system starts SLA timer per order
Responsible (R): System / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: &lt; 5 min (system routing)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1429_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1429_Task6" name="Real-time SLA monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Real-time SLA monitoring (T+0 to T+4 hours): (a) E-Commerce Operations Manager monitors BOPIS SLA dashboard: (i) orders in progress with time remaining, (ii) orders approaching SLA breach (&lt; 1 hour remaining and not yet picked), (iii) orders breached (4-hour SLA exceeded without pick completion), (b) SLA compliance rate by store: identify stores consistently breaching SLA (&gt; 10% breach rate in a week), (c) system auto-escalates: (i) T+2 hours and not started: yellow alert to Store Manager via mobile app, (ii) T+3 hours and not completed: red alert to Store Manager with instruction to prioritize immediately, (iii) T+4 hours (breach): automatic escalation to E-Commerce Operations Manager + customer notification
Responsible (R): System / E-Commerce Operations Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: Continuous (dashboard review: 2–3 hours/day)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1429_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1429_Task7" name="Exception handling for SLA breaches">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Exception handling for SLA breaches: When an order breaches the 4-hour SLA: (a) E-Commerce Operations Manager investigates root cause: (i) store staffing shortage (not enough Stock Associates on shift), (ii) item not found at expected location (inventory inaccuracy — shelf empty but system shows stock), (iii) bulky item handling delay (yard item requires forklift), (iv) high BOPIS volume day (e.g., payday weekend) overwhelming pick capacity, (b) resolution options: (i) expedite pick immediately (reassign from another task), (ii) if item genuinely unavailable: initiate short-ship (pick available items, cancel unavailable with customer notification and partial refund), (iii) if delay is &lt; 2 additional hours: pick and send delayed-ready notification with apology
Responsible (R): E-Commerce Operations Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 15–30 min/exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1429_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1429_Task8" name="Customer notification management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer notification management: System sends automated customer notifications: (a) order received: confirmation email/SMS with order number and pickup location, (b) pick in progress: (no customer notification — internal only), (c) ready for pickup: email/SMS/push notification — &quot;Your order is ready! Please bring valid ID and order confirmation to Customer Service Counter at [Store Name]. Your order will be held for 5 days.&quot;, (d) SLA breach apology (if applicable): &quot;We&#x27;re sorry — your order is taking longer than expected. We&#x27;re working on it and will notify you as soon as it&#x27;s ready.&quot;, (e) order aging (5 days with no pickup): reminder notification per W771 — &quot;Your order will be auto-cancelled in [X] days. Please pick up or contact us to extend.&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): E-Commerce Operations Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1429_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1429_Task9" name="Weekly SLA performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly SLA performance review: (a) E-Commerce Operations Manager reviews weekly BOPIS SLA metrics: (i) chain-wide SLA compliance rate (target: ≥ 95%), (ii) SLA compliance by store (identify bottom 10 stores), (iii) SLA compliance by day of week (payday weekends vs. weekdays), (iv) top reasons for SLA breach (staffing, stockout, volume), (b) for stores with &lt; 90% SLA compliance: Store Manager must submit corrective action plan (e.g., assign dedicated BOPIS picker during peak hours), (c) trend analysis: is SLA compliance improving or deteriorating?
Responsible (R): E-Commerce Operations Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1429_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1429_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
