    <bpmn:process id="W_W1442" name="W1442. BOPIS Customer No-Show Rate Monitoring, Auto-Cancel Processing &amp; Restocking Workflow" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: BOPIS order hold period expires (5 days) without customer pickup; or daily no-show rate monitoring dashboard alert
Frequency: ~8–12% no-show rate = ~2,000–3,100 orders/month across all 200 stores; daily auto-cancel processing; weekly no-show rate review
Volume: ~25,700 BOPIS orders/month; ~2,000–3,100 no-shows/month; each no-show triggers auto-cancel, refund, and restock
Owner: E-Commerce Operations Manager
Participants: E-Commerce Ops Manager, Store Customer Service Rep, Finance/AP (refund processing), Stock Associate (restocking)
Source: workflow W1442 — BOPIS Customer No-Show Rate Monitoring, Auto-Cancel Processing &amp; Restocking Workflow</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1442_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1442_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1442_Lane2" name="Customer Service Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1442_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1442_Lane4" name="E-Commerce Ops Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1442_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1442_Start6" name="BOPIS order hold period expires (5 days) without customer pickup; or daily no-show rate…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1442_Task7" name="Proactive customer reminders">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Proactive customer reminders: System sends automated reminders to BOPIS customers: (a) Day 1 (order placed): confirmation email/SMS with pickup instructions, store hours, and required ID, (b) Day 3 (if not picked up): reminder email/SMS — &quot;Your order is ready for pickup! Please pick up within 2 days&quot;, (c) Day 4 (if not picked up): final reminder — &quot;Last day! Your order will be auto-cancelled tomorrow at [time] and refunded&quot;, (d) customer can extend hold period by 2 days via app/email reply (one extension allowed)
Responsible (R): System (automated)
Accountable (A): E-Commerce Ops Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1442_Task8" name="Daily auto-cancel processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily auto-cancel processing: At end of Day 5 (hold period expiry): (a) system auto-cancels all unpicked BOPIS orders, (b) system initiates refund to original payment method (credit card, e-wallet, GCash), (c) system generates daily auto-cancel report: order number, SKU, store, value, cancel reason (&quot;hold period expired&quot;), (d) system releases inventory reservation — items become available for walk-in sale
Responsible (R): System (automated)
Accountable (A): E-Commerce Ops Manager
Duration: Automated (30 min/day exception review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1442_Task9" name="Customer service follow-up for high-value orders">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer service follow-up for high-value orders: For auto-cancelled orders &gt; PHP 10,000: (a) E-Commerce Ops Manager flags for manual review — verify customer did not attempt pickup (sometimes system error), (b) Customer Service Rep contacts customer via phone: (i) apologize for any inconvenience, (ii) offer to reorder with expedited processing, (iii) document reason for no-show (forgot, changed mind, found cheaper elsewhere, emergency), (c) if customer wants to reorder: create new BOPIS order with priority pick status
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): E-Commerce Ops Manager
Duration: 10 min per high-value order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1442_Task10" name="Restocking execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Restocking execution: Stock Associate restocks auto-cancelled items: (a) retrieve item from BOPIS staging area, (b) verify item condition (no damage from staging), (c) return to shelf location per planogram, (d) system updates on-hand inventory — item now available for walk-in and ecommerce sale, (e) for large/bulky items (appliances, lumber): restock priority is high to free staging space
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1442_Task11" name="Weekly no-show rate analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly no-show rate analysis: E-Commerce Ops Manager reviews weekly no-show dashboard: (a) no-show rate by store (identify stores with &gt; 15% rate for root cause analysis), (b) no-show rate by category (identify product types customers frequently abandon), (c) no-show rate by day-of-week and time (identify patterns), (d) customer demographics of no-shows (new vs. repeat, loyalty tier), (e) revenue impact of no-shows: refund processing cost + lost walk-in sales from reserved inventory, (f) implement corrective actions: adjust hold period, tighten payment authorization, require deposit for high-value BOPIS
Responsible (R): E-Commerce Ops Manager
Accountable (A): E-Commerce Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1442_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1442_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1442_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1442_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-270 (ensure controlled execution — Order Fulfillment &amp; Delivery (PA-10.2).) | - operational: E-Commerce Operations Manager review and approval gate
Owner: E-Commerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1442_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1442_Annotation13" targetRef="W1442_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1442_Flow15" sourceRef="W1442_Start6" targetRef="W1442_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1442_Flow16" sourceRef="W1442_Task7" targetRef="W1442_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1442_Flow17" sourceRef="W1442_Task8" targetRef="W1442_Task9" />
